    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "217429028b3d981e9a182d77260eca5c8d72950a88b6b74944f9599b025887d4",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel.\nDepart to Yaxchilan an ancient Mayan archaeological site located in the dense rainforests of Chiapas, located along the Usumacinta River, making it accessible only by boat. This site is renowed for its intricately carved stone lintels and stelae wich depict the history and mythology of the Mayan civilization.\nAfterward we will visit Bonampak, an archaeological site located in the dense jungles of the Chiapas region in southern Mexico. Renowned for its exceptionally well-preserved ancient murals, Bonampak provides a captivating glimpse into the artistic and cultural achievements of the Maya civilization. Bonampak's archaeological remains include plazas, ball courts, and residential structures, contributing to our understanding of Maya urban planning and societal structures.\nIn the afternoon return to Palenque for the overnight.",
